msgstr "← Manage"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.department_manager.help"
msgstr "A user holding this role is a department director of every department their group mappings place them in. Leave empty to disable."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.department_manager.label"
msgstr "Department director role ID"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.global_admin.help"
msgstr "A user holding this role becomes a global admin across the whole app. Leave empty to disable."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.global_admin.label"
msgstr "Global admin role ID"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.shift_manager.help"
msgstr "As above, for shift managers. A user holding both roles becomes a department director."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.shift_manager.label"
msgstr "Shift manager role ID"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.sub_admin.help"
msgstr "A user holding this role becomes a sub admin. A user holding both this and the global admin role becomes a global admin."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.field.sub_admin.label"
msgstr "Sub admin role ID"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.global.intro"
msgstr "These roles are app-wide, not tied to any department. A user holding the global admin role becomes a global admin; the sub admin role makes them a sub admin. Holding both resolves to <strong>global admin</strong> - the higher role wins."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.global.note"
msgstr "Each grant is re-evaluated on every sign-in, so losing a role at the identity provider strips it on the next login. Leave a field blank to have the app ignore that group entirely - a membership you granted by hand is then left untouched."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.global.title"
msgstr "Global roles"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.page.subtitle"
msgstr "Which identity-provider roles grant SSO users a department position or global admin rights."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.page.title"
msgstr "SSO Roles"

msgid "admin.sso.roles.positions.intro"
msgstr "A group mapping puts a user <em>in</em> a department. These two roles decide <em>what they are</em> there - the same pair applies to every department."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.positions.item.department_manager"
msgstr "<strong>Department director</strong> - holds the department director role and a department role."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.positions.item.department_staff"
msgstr "<strong>Department staff</strong> - holds a department role only."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.positions.item.shift_manager"
msgstr "<strong>Shift manager</strong> - holds the shift manager role and a department role."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.positions.note"
msgstr "Holding both roles makes the user a department director. Positions are re-evaluated on every sign-in, so removing a role at the identity provider demotes the user on their next login."

msgid "admin.sso.roles.positions.title"
msgstr "Department positions"

